    "created_at": "2016-08-17T05:55:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-17T05:55:45Z",
    "body": "I looked for cases where Blink looks at the (internal) `nodeType` and not taking the same code path for `TEXT_NODE` and `CDATA_SECTION_NODE` and found two more things:\n1. Range::surroundContents would throw if a CDATASection node is partially contained. That's unlikely to be intentional.\n2. Two \"FIXME: What about kCdataSectionNode?\" in the editing code that check `nodeType` seemingly specifically to exclude CDATASection.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
